# Work-machine ~/.ssh/config
#
# Written fresh. NOTHING is carried over from the personal config, which pointed
# at a different forge with a Linux IdentityFile path that does not exist here.
#
# Two deliberate differences from the personal version:
#
#   1. No `StrictHostKeyChecking no`. That disables host-key verification, which
#      is the check that protects against a man-in-the-middle. It is worth
#      removing on personal machines too.
#   2. UseKeychain + AddKeysToAgent are macOS-only (Apple's OpenSSH fork). They
#      let the passphrase live in the login keychain instead of being retyped or,
#      worse, omitted.
#
# NEVER copy a private key between machines. setup-work-configs.sh generates a
# fresh ed25519 pair; upload only the .pub half to whatever forge work uses.

Host *
	AddKeysToAgent yes
	UseKeychain yes
	IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_work
	IdentitiesOnly yes
	ServerAliveInterval 60

# Add work forge hosts below once you know where their code lives, e.g.
#
# Host github.com
# 	User git
# 	IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_work
